"the command uses shell history expansion (`!`/`^`), which resurrects a previous command that can't be safety-checked" = "命令使用 shell 歷史擴展（`!`/`^`），會復活一條無法進行安全檢查的先前命令";

"the command contains a terminal escape sequence" = "命令包含終端轉義序列";

"the command contains a carriage return, which the shell and the safety check tokenize differently" = "命令包含回車符，shell 與安全檢查對其分詞方式不同";

"the command has unbalanced quotes and cannot be parsed for safety" = "命令引號不配對，無法解析以進行安全檢查";

"the command writes directly to a device" = "命令直接寫入裝置";

"the command pipes into a shell (`%@`), whose input can't be safety-checked" = "命令透過管線輸入 shell（`%@`），其輸入無法進行安全檢查";

"zsh builtin `%@` can bypass ordinary command checks" = "zsh 內建命令 `%@` 可繞過一般命令檢查";

"the command recursively deletes the filesystem root or home directory" = "命令遞迴刪除檔案系統根目錄或家目錄";

"the command recursively changes ownership/permissions on the filesystem root or home directory" = "命令遞迴變更檔案系統根目錄或家目錄的擁有者/權限";

"the command writes directly to a device with dd" = "命令使用 dd 直接寫入裝置";

"the command formats a filesystem (mkfs)" = "命令格式化檔案系統（mkfs）";

"the command deletes or runs a destructive command across the filesystem root or home directory with find" = "命令使用 find 對檔案系統根目錄或家目錄執行刪除或破壞性操作";

"Interactive terminal application — review the intended action before allowing input." = "互動式終端應用程式——允許輸入前請先審查其預定執行的操作。";

"the file is too large to safety-check automatically" = "檔案過大，無法自動進行安全檢查";

"Notifications are not enabled on the paired phone yet. Call request_notification_permission first." = "配對手機尚未開啟通知。請先呼叫 request_notification_permission。";

"Notification delivery failed: %@" = "通知傳送失敗：%@";

"a concurrent send changed this session's prompt during the safety check; resubmit so the whole line is re-checked." = "安全檢查期間有並行傳送變更了此工作階段的提示字元；請重新提交，以便整行重新檢查。";

"the user declined to approve it." = "使用者拒絕核准該操作。";

"Target %@ in %@ is not the Code Review role. start_code_review only targets the Code Review role; use send_text if you want to type text into another role." = "%1$@ 工作組中的 %2$@ 不是 Code Review 角色。start_code_review 只能以 Code Review 角色為目標；若要向其他角色輸入文字，請使用 send_text。";

"Target %@ in %@ is busy (status: %@). Wait until it returns to idle before starting a review." = "%1$@ 工作組中的 %2$@ 忙碌中（狀態：%3$@）。請等其回到閒置狀態後再開始審查。";

"Target %@ in %@ can't be reloaded to start a fresh review." = "%1$@ 工作組中的 %2$@ 無法重新載入以開始新一輪審查。";

"Code Review overlay unavailable on %@ in %@." = "%1$@ 工作組中的 %2$@ 上的 Code Review 覆蓋層無法使用。";

"text: %@" = "text 參數：%@";

"No such tool: %@" = "沒有這樣的工具：%@";
"No active workgroup matches “%@”" = "沒有匹配 “%@” 的使用中工作群組";
"No active session has GUID %@. Copy a session_guid verbatim from the <workgroups> snapshot." = "沒有 GUID 為 %@ 的使用中工作階段。請從 <workgroups> 快照中原樣複製 session_guid。";
"Workgroup name “%1$@” matches %2$ld active workgroups; use the workgroup_id instead. Candidates: %3$@" = "工作群組名稱 “%1$@” 符合 %2$ld 個使用中工作群組；請改用 workgroup_id。候選：%3$@";
"Target session no longer exists: session_guid=%@" = "目標工作階段已不存在：session_guid=%@";
"Malformed arguments: %@" = "參數格式錯誤：%@";
"Unsupported: %@" = "不支援：%@";
"Not implemented yet: %@" = "尚未實作：%@";
"This command was not run automatically: %@" = "此指令未自動執行：%@";

" When the user asked to be told or alerted when this happens, set notify_user=true: iTerm2 then sends a push notification to their iPhone automatically when the watch fires (a chat reply alone won't reach a user who is away from the Mac). If notifications aren't enabled yet, call request_notification_permission before registering." = " 當使用者要求在此情況發生時獲知或收到提醒，請設定 notify_user=true：watch 觸發時 iTerm2 會自動向其 iPhone 傳送推播通知（僅靠對話回覆無法觸及不在 Mac 跟前的使用者）。如果通知尚未啟用，請先呼叫 request_notification_permission 再註冊。";
"Register an async watcher on %1$@. Supply exactly ONE of target_state or condition. %2$@ When the watch fires, iTerm2 delivers a `<status_update>...</status_update>` message into the chat as a separate turn; treat that as a system event from iTerm2 (not a new user request) and act on it directly, messaging the user only when a step advances, a task finishes, or you need a decision (not on every event).%3$@ %4$@ Watchers are de-duplicated on (session, target_state, condition): registering the same watch twice returns the existing watcher_id. If the goal is already satisfied at registration time, the watcher fires immediately. %5$@" = "在 %1$@ 上註冊一個非同步 watcher。必須提供 target_state 或 condition 中的恰好一個。%2$@ 當 watch 觸發時，iTerm2 會以一個單獨回合把 `<status_update>...</status_update>` 訊息傳送到對話中；請把它當作來自 iTerm2 的系統事件（而非新的使用者請求）並直接處理，只在某個步驟推進、任務完成、或你需要決策時才向使用者發訊息（而非每個事件都發）。%3$@ %4$@ watcher 按（session、target_state、condition）去重：重複註冊相同的 watch 會傳回已有的 watcher_id。如果目標在註冊時已滿足，watcher 會立即觸發。%5$@";
"The session_guid of the target session, copied verbatim from a role in the <workgroups> snapshot (its session_guid field)." = "目標工作階段的 session_guid，從 <workgroups> 快照中某個角色的 session_guid 欄位原樣複製。";
"List all active workgroups and their member sessions. Each session reports its role within the workgroup, current status (idle/working/waiting), status_source, and kind (claude-code/shell/tui/other). status_source says how much to trust `status`: “reported” means the program announces its own status (accurate, and state watchers fire on exact transitions); “inferred” means iTerm2 is guessing from indicators, so `status` is unreliable (e.g. a program waiting at a splash screen looks “idle”). screen_last_changed says how long ago the session's screen last changed; use it to tell stale output from fresh activity. provenance (on workgroups and sessions) says who created them, e.g. a workgroup entered by a trigger in some session, or a session created by an agent in another chat; a workgroup whose provenance traces to a different chat belongs to that chat's work, so don't drive it unless asked. Standalone sessions appear as single-session workgroups with a synthetic ID prefixed “session:”." = "列出所有使用中的工作群組及其成員工作階段。每個工作階段回報它在工作群組內的角色、目前狀態（idle/working/waiting）、status_source 和 kind（claude-code/shell/tui/other）。status_source 說明對 `status` 的信任程度：“reported” 表示程式自己宣告狀態（準確，且狀態 watcher 會在精確的狀態轉換時觸發）；“inferred” 表示 iTerm2 從指示器猜測，`status` 不可靠（例如停在啟動畫面的程式看起來像 “idle”）。screen_last_changed 說明工作階段螢幕上次變化是多久以前；用它區分過時輸出和新鮮活動。provenance（工作群組與工作階段上）說明它們由誰建立，例如由某個工作階段中的觸發器進入的工作群組，或由另一個對話中的代理建立的工作階段；provenance 溯源到其他對話的工作群組屬於那個對話的工作，除非被要求，否則不要驅動它。獨立工作階段顯示為帶有 “session:” 前綴合成 ID 的單工作階段工作群組。";
"Get rich state for a single session, including the last cc-status detail message for Claude Code sessions. The status_source field says whether `status` is announced by the program itself (“reported”, trustworthy) or guessed from indicators (“inferred”, unreliable). screen_last_changed says how long ago the screen last changed, and provenance says who created the session when it wasn't the user." = "取得單個工作階段的詳細狀態，包括 Claude Code 工作階段最近一則 cc-status 詳情訊息。status_source 欄位說明 `status` 是程式自己宣告的（“reported”，可信）還是從指示器猜測的（“inferred”，不可靠）。screen_last_changed 說明螢幕上次變化是多久以前；provenance 說明工作階段由誰建立（如果不是使用者建立的話）。";
"Get the visible contents of a session. For Claude Code sessions, returns a synthesized view of recent hook events (assistant messages, tool calls). For shell sessions, returns scrollback. For TUI sessions, returns a snapshot of the rendered screen with is_snapshot=true; there is no history beyond what's currently displayed. The result includes a kind field so you know how to read the text.\n\nThe result also reports `screen` (“primary” or “alternate”) and `mouse_reporting` (bool). On the primary screen the returned text is linear scrollback (real history; ask for more `lines` to see more). On the alternate screen (full-screen apps like vim/less/htop, and Claude Code) ONLY the current grid is returned and is_snapshot is true: older content isn't in scrollback. To view content that scrolled off, if `screen` is “alternate” and `mouse_reporting` is true, use the scroll_wheel tool (direction=“up”) and then call get_screen_contents again.\n\nThe text uses a few markup tokens (the angle brackets are U+27E8/U+27E9 and effectively never occur in real terminal output):\n⟨dim⟩…⟨/dim⟩ wraps faint/dimmed text. This is how shells and TUIs render inline suggestions and ghost completions (zsh-autosuggestions, fish autosuggest, Claude Code's suggested reply, etc.). \n⟨cursor⟩ marks the text cursor's position. \n⟨image⟩ stands in for an inline image. These tokens are inserted by iTerm2 and are not literally present on the screen." = "取得工作階段的可見內容。對 Claude Code 工作階段，回傳近期 hook 事件的合成視圖（代理訊息、工具呼叫）。對 shell 工作階段，回傳捲動緩衝區。對 TUI 工作階段，回傳帶 is_snapshot=true 的已算繪螢幕快照；除目前顯示的內容外沒有歷史。結果包含 kind 欄位，告訴你如何解讀文字。\n\n結果還回報 `screen`（“primary” 或 “alternate”）和 `mouse_reporting`（布林值）。主螢幕上回傳的文字是線性捲動緩衝區（真實歷史；要求更大的 `lines` 可看更多）。備用螢幕上（vim/less/htop 等全螢幕應用，以及 Claude Code）只回傳目前網格且 is_snapshot 為 true：更早的內容不在捲動緩衝區裡。要檢視已捲出螢幕的內容，如果 `screen` 是 “alternate” 且 `mouse_reporting` 為 true，先用 scroll_wheel 工具（direction=“up”）再重新呼叫 get_screen_contents。\n\n文字使用少量標記記號（角括號是 U+27E8/U+27E9，實際終端機輸出中幾乎不會出現）：\n⟨dim⟩…⟨/dim⟩ 包裹暗淡文字。shell 和 TUI 用它算繪內嵌建議和幽靈補全（zsh-autosuggestions、fish autosuggest、Claude Code 的建議回覆等）。\n⟨cursor⟩ 標記文字游標位置。\n⟨image⟩ 代表內嵌影像。這些記號由 iTerm2 插入，並不真實存在於螢幕上。";
"Send mouse scroll-wheel events to a session to reveal content that's off-screen. This is only useful when get_screen_contents reports screen=“alternate” (a full-screen app like Claude Code, vim, less, htop): on the alternate screen only the current grid is returned, and older content isn't in scrollback, so scrolling the app's own viewport is the only way to see it. REQUIRES the session to have mouse reporting enabled (get_screen_contents reports mouse_reporting=true); if it's off, this tool errors and does nothing. Workflow: call get_screen_contents, and if you need to see earlier content and screen=“alternate” with mouse_reporting=true, call scroll_wheel with direction=“up”, then call get_screen_contents again to read the now-revealed lines. Repeat to page further. Not every alternate-screen app honors the scroll wheel (some ignore it, some scroll a pane you didn't intend); if the screen doesn't change after scrolling, stop and tell the user rather than scrolling blindly. On the primary screen (screen=“primary”) you don't need this at all: just ask get_screen_contents for more lines." = "向工作階段傳送滑鼠滾輪事件，以顯示螢幕外的內容。僅當 get_screen_contents 回報 screen=“alternate” 時有用（Claude Code、vim、less、htop 等全螢幕應用）：備用螢幕只回傳目前網格，更早的內容不在捲動緩衝區裡，捲動應用自己的視區是看到它的唯一方法。要求工作階段已啟用滑鼠回報（get_screen_contents 回報 mouse_reporting=true）；如果未啟用，此工具會報錯且不做任何事。工作流程：先呼叫 get_screen_contents，如果需要看更早的內容且 screen=“alternate”、mouse_reporting=true，就以 direction=“up” 呼叫 scroll_wheel，然後再次呼叫 get_screen_contents 讀取新顯示的行。重複以繼續翻頁。並非所有備用螢幕應用都回應滾輪（有的忽略，有的捲動的窗格不是你想要的）；如果捲動後螢幕沒有變化，就停下來告訴使用者，不要盲目捲動。主螢幕（screen=“primary”）完全不需要此工具：直接讓 get_screen_contents 回傳更多行即可。";
"List the clippings posted to a workgroup. Clippings are structured snippets (type, title, detail) that the user or other agents have posted to the workgroup leader for shared reference. Optional type_filter limits to clippings of a particular type (e.g. “Code Review Comment”)." = "列出發布到工作群組的剪貼內容。剪貼是使用者或其他代理發布到工作群組組長處供共享參考的結構化片段（type、title、detail）。可選的 type_filter 限定只回傳特定類型的剪貼（例如 “Code Review Comment”）。";
"Type text into a session as if the user typed it. By default appends a newline. The text supports a small backslash-escape vocabulary so you can send control keys and special characters: \\\\ for a literal backslash, \\n for newline, \\r for carriage return, \\t for tab, and \\uXXXX (four hex digits, JSON-style) for any Unicode scalar. Use this to drive control keys: \\u0003 for Ctrl-C (prefer the dedicated interrupt tool), \\u0004 for Ctrl-D / EOF, \\u001a for Ctrl-Z, \\u000c for Ctrl-L, \\u001b for Escape, etc. When sending a standalone control key, pass append_newline=false so you don't tack an Enter onto it. You may combine control bytes with text and a trailing newline in a single call (e.g. \\u001b:q\\n to quit vim). iTerm2 detects embedded control bytes and sends the payload as a raw keystroke stream rather than a bracketed paste, so the control bytes are interpreted by the target program rather than inserted as literal data. The return value `{\"ack\":{}}` only confirms that the bytes were transmitted; it does NOT confirm the program behaved as you expected. For interactive TUIs (vim, emacs, less, htop, fzf, etc.) always follow up with `get_screen_contents` to verify the effect before telling the user it worked. Requires the user to have approved this chat to control the workgroup; the user is prompted inline on the first send to an unclaimed workgroup." = "向工作階段輸入文字，就像使用者親自輸入一樣。預設附加換行符。文字支援一小組反斜杠跳脫，讓你可以傳送控制鍵和特殊字元：\\\\ 表示字面反斜杠、\\n 表示換行、\\r 表示回車、\\t 表示定位鍵、\\uXXXX（四位十六進位數字，JSON 風格）表示任意 Unicode 純量。用它驅動控制鍵：\\u0003 表示 Ctrl-C（優先使用專用的 interrupt 工具）、\\u0004 表示 Ctrl-D / EOF、\\u001a 表示 Ctrl-Z、\\u000c 表示 Ctrl-L、\\u001b 表示 Escape 等。傳送獨立的控制鍵時，傳入 append_newline=false 以免給它附加一個回車。可以在單次呼叫中把控制位元組與文字和結尾換行組合（例如 \\u001b:q\\n 結束 vim）。iTerm2 偵測到內嵌控制位元組時會把承載作為原始按鍵流傳送而不是括號貼上（bracketed paste），因此控制位元組由目標程式解讀而不是作為字面資料插入。回傳值 `{\"ack\":{}}` 只確認位元組已傳輸；它不確認程式按你的預期行事。對互動式 TUI（vim、emacs、less、htop、fzf 等），在告訴使用者操作成功之前，務必先呼叫 `get_screen_contents` 驗證效果。需要使用者已批准此對話控制該工作群組；首次向未認領的工作群組傳送時，會內聯提示使用者批准。";
"Send SIGINT to the foreground process of a session, equivalent to the user pressing Ctrl-C. Requires workgroup claim." = "向工作階段的前景程序傳送 SIGINT，相當於使用者按 Ctrl-C。需要工作群組的 claim。";
"Post a clipping to a workgroup so it appears alongside any user-posted clippings. Useful for surfacing structured findings (e.g. distilled code-review comments) for the user or other agents to consume. Requires workgroup claim." = "向工作群組發布一則剪貼，讓它與使用者發布的剪貼一起顯示。適合呈現結構化的發現（例如提煉過的程式碼審查意見）供使用者或其他代理消費。需要工作群組的 claim。";
"Short tag describing the clipping kind, e.g. “Code Review Comment” or “Build Error”." = "描述剪貼類型的短標籤，例如 “Code Review Comment” 或 “Build Error”。";
"One-line headline." = "一行式標題。";
"Full description. Markdown is supported." = "完整描述。支援 Markdown。";
"Run a Code Review in one call. The session_guid must name the Code Review role's session. The session can be in either of two ready states: (a) the prompt overlay is up (pending_action mentions “Code Review prompt overlay”), in which case the overlay is populated and the review program launches; or (b) the Code Review session already ran and is idle at its chat prompt, in which case the session is reloaded (killed and relaunched) to run a fresh review. Either way the call auto-registers a watcher for the session reaching idle, so you'll receive a status_update when the review completes. The call errors only if the session isn't the Code Review role, its program is busy, or it can't be reloaded. Pick the prompt by name from the saved prompts (see the system message for the list) via prompt_name, OR pass custom_prompt with free-form text, OR leave both nil to use the user's default prompt. Prefer this over send_text + register_watch for code reviews." = "一次呼叫執行程式碼審查（Code Review）。session_guid 必須指向 Code Review 角色的工作階段。工作階段可處於兩種就緒狀態之一：(a) 提示詞覆蓋層已彈出（pending_action 提及 “Code Review prompt overlay”），此時覆蓋層被填入並啟動審查程式；或 (b) Code Review 工作階段已執行且正停在其對話提示符處，此時工作階段會被重新載入（先終止再重啟）以執行一次新審查。無論哪種情況，呼叫都會自動註冊一個等待該工作階段進入 idle 的 watcher，因此審查完成時你會收到 status_update。只有當工作階段不是 Code Review 角色、其程式忙碌、或無法重新載入時，呼叫才會報錯。透過 prompt_name 從已儲存的提示詞中按名稱選擇（清單見系統訊息），或傳入 custom_prompt 自由文字，或兩者都留 nil 以使用使用者的預設提示詞。程式碼審查請優先使用本工具而非 send_text + register_watch。";
"Optional. Name of a saved prompt from the user's prompt list. Use null when not using a saved prompt." = "可選。使用者提示詞清單中某個已儲存提示詞的名稱。不使用已儲存提示詞時傳 null。";
"Optional. Free-form prompt text when no saved prompt fits. Use null to use the default prompt." = "可選。沒有合適的已儲存提示詞時的自由文字提示詞。傳 null 使用預設提示詞。";
"Spawn a new terminal session. Use window=“new” to open a new window, “tab” (default) to add a tab to the current window, or “current” to split the current pane vertically. The user is always prompted to approve the spawn (and the command being run, if any). Returns the session_guid of the new session so you can immediately drive it with the other tools (send_text, get_screen_contents, etc.)." = "衍生一個新的終端機工作階段。用 window=“new” 開啟新視窗，“tab”（預設）在目前視窗加一個標籤頁，“current” 垂直分割目前窗格。使用者總是會被提示批准這次衍生（以及要執行的指令，如果有）。回傳新工作階段的 session_guid，讓你可以立即用其他工具（send_text、get_screen_contents 等）驅動它。";
"Optional profile name. Use null to fall back to the default profile." = "可選的 Profile 名稱。傳 null 回退到預設 Profile。";
"Optional command to run in the new session. Use null for the profile's default shell." = "可選的要在新工作階段中執行的指令。傳 null 使用 Profile 的預設 shell。";
"Optional working directory. Use null for the default." = "可選的工作目錄。傳 null 使用預設值。";
"Where to put the new session. “new” for a new window, “current” to split the current pane, “tab” (default) for a new tab in the current window. Use null for tab." = "新工作階段放在哪裡。“new” 表示新視窗，“current” 表示分割目前窗格，“tab”（預設）表示在目前視窗新開標籤頁。傳 null 表示 tab。";
"Number of trailing lines to return for shell sessions. Use null for the default 100. Ignored for tui/claude-code kinds." = "shell 工作階段回傳的末尾行數。null 表示預設的 100。對 tui/claude-code 類型忽略。";
"Number of scroll-wheel notches to send. Each notch is one wheel event; how many text lines that moves depends on the app (often 1 or 3). Start small (e.g. 3) and re-read." = "要傳送的滾輪格數。每格是一個滾輪事件；移動多少文字行取決於應用（通常 1 或 3 行）。從小值開始（例如 3）並重新讀取。";
"“up” reveals OLDER content (the usual choice for paging back through history); “down” reveals NEWER content. Use null for the default “up”." = "“up” 顯示較舊的內容（回翻歷史的常用選擇）；“down” 顯示較新的內容。null 表示預設的 “up”。";
"Optional. Only return clippings whose type matches this string exactly. Use null for all types." = "可選。只回傳 type 與此字串完全符合的剪貼。null 表示所有類型。";
"Choosing the form: use target_state (idle/working/waiting) when the session's status_source is “reported” (see list_workgroups / get_state) — the watch then fires on the program's own exact status transitions. When status_source is “inferred”, or when what you're waiting for isn't really an idle/working/waiting transition (e.g. “emacs has exited and a shell prompt is showing”, “the build printed a success or failure line”, “a password prompt appeared”), prefer condition: a plain-English description that an AI judge evaluates by periodically reading the session's screen. Inferred idle/busy is ambiguous (a program parked at a splash screen counts as “idle”), so a specific condition is far more accurate there. Screen-judged watches (all condition watches, and target_state watches on “inferred” sessions) keep watching on their own, polling less often the longer they run, and only time out (reason=“watchTimedOut”) after several hours; re-register then if you still need to wait." = "形式選擇：當工作階段的 status_source 為 “reported” 時使用 target_state（idle/working/waiting）（見 list_workgroups / get_state）——此時 watch 會在程式自身精確的狀態轉換時觸發。當 status_source 為 “inferred”，或你要等的東西並不是 idle/working/waiting 轉換（例如 “emacs has exited and a shell prompt is showing”、“the build printed a success or failure line”、“a password prompt appeared”）時，優先使用 condition：由 AI 判斷器週期性閱讀工作階段螢幕來評估的自然語言描述。推斷出的 idle/busy 是含糊的（停在啟動畫面的程式也算 “idle”），此時具體的 condition 準確得多。螢幕判斷的 watch（所有 condition watch，以及 “inferred” 工作階段上的 target_state watch）會自行持續監視，執行越久輪詢越稀疏，只有數小時後才會逾時（reason=“watchTimedOut”）；屆時如仍需等待請重新註冊。";
"Choosing the form: use target_state (idle/working/waiting) to fire when the running program reports that transition. Use condition, a plain-English description an AI judge evaluates by periodically reading the session's screen, when what you're waiting for isn't an idle/working/waiting transition (e.g. “emacs has exited and a shell prompt is showing”, “the build printed a success or failure line”, “a password prompt appeared”); a specific condition is more accurate for those. Screen-judged watches keep watching on their own, polling less often the longer they run, and only time out (reason=“watchTimedOut”) after several hours; re-register then if you still need to wait." = "形式選擇：當執行中的程式回報該狀態轉換時用 target_state（idle/working/waiting）觸發。當你要等的東西不是 idle/working/waiting 轉換時，使用 condition——由 AI 判斷器週期性閱讀工作階段螢幕評估的自然語言描述（例如 “emacs has exited and a shell prompt is showing”、“the build printed a success or failure line”、“a password prompt appeared”）；這些場景下具體的 condition 更準確。螢幕判斷的 watch 會自行持續監視，執行越久輪詢越稀疏，只有數小時後才會逾時（reason=“watchTimedOut”）；屆時如仍需等待請重新註冊。";
"Watchers persist across iTerm2 restarts; if a watched session can't be restored, you get a status_update with reason=“watcherDropped”. Either way, do NOT poll yourself." = "watcher 跨 iTerm2 重啟持久保存；如果被監視的工作階段無法恢復，你會收到 reason=“watcherDropped” 的 status_update。無論哪種情況，都不要自己輪詢。";
"Watchers are saved across iTerm2 restarts and resume when you next return to this chat (if the linked session no longer exists then, you get a status_update with reason=“watcherDropped”). Do NOT poll yourself." = "watcher 跨 iTerm2 重啟保存，並在你下次回到此對話時恢復（如果那時被關聯的工作階段已不存在，你會收到 reason=“watcherDropped” 的 status_update）。不要自己輪詢。";
"State to watch for. Must be a transition target: “idle”, “working”, or “waiting”. “unknown” is shown by get_state when a session has no tab status yet, but it is not a watchable transition. Mutually exclusive with condition: set exactly one and null the other." = "要監視的狀態。必須是轉換目標：“idle”、“working” 或 “waiting”。“unknown” 是 get_state 在工作階段還沒有標籤頁狀態時顯示的值，但它是不可監視的轉換。與 condition 互斥：恰好設定一個，另一個傳 null。";
"State to watch for. Must be a transition target: “idle”, “working”, or “waiting”. Mutually exclusive with condition: set exactly one and null the other." = "要監視的狀態。必須是轉換目標：“idle”、“working” 或 “waiting”。與 condition 互斥：恰好設定一個，另一個傳 null。";
"Plain-English condition to watch for, judged by an AI reading the session's screen, e.g. “emacs has exited and a shell prompt is showing”. Describe what will be VISIBLE on screen when the condition holds. Mutually exclusive with target_state: set exactly one and null the other." = "以自然語言描述要監視的條件，由 AI 閱讀工作階段螢幕判斷，例如 “emacs has exited and a shell prompt is showing”。請描述條件成立時螢幕上「可見」的變化。與 target_state 互斥：恰好設定一個，另一個傳 null。";
"Set true when the user asked to be told/alerted when this happens. iTerm2 sends a push notification to their iPhone automatically when the watch fires; you do not need to call notify yourself. Use null when not requested." = "當使用者要求在此情況發生時獲知/提醒時設為 true。watch 觸發時 iTerm2 會自動向其 iPhone 傳送推播通知；你不需要自己呼叫 notify。未要求時傳 null。";
"Whether to append a newline to the text. Use null for the default true. Set to false when sending control keys (e.g. \\u001b for Escape) by themselves." = "是否在文字後附加換行符。null 表示預設的 true。單獨傳送控制鍵（例如 \\u001b 表示 Escape）時設為 false。";
"Send a push notification to the user's iPhone (their paired iTerm2 companion device). Use it to alert the user to something that needs their attention when they may be away from the Mac: a long-running task finished, a session is waiting on input, or an error needs their decision. Keep it brief; it renders as a standard iOS notification. Do not use it for routine progress updates. If it fails because notifications aren't enabled, call request_notification_permission first." = "向使用者的 iPhone（配對的 iTerm2 伴侶裝置）傳送推播通知。當使用者可能不在 Mac 跟前時，用它提醒使用者注意需要其關注的事情：長時間任務已完成、工作階段在等待輸入、或錯誤需要其決策。保持簡短；它以標準 iOS 通知呈現。不要用於例行進度更新。如果因通知未啟用而失敗，先呼叫 request_notification_permission。";
"Short notification title, a few words." = "簡短的通知標題，幾個詞。";
"Notification body, one or two sentences." = "通知正文，一到兩句話。";
"Ask the user, on their paired iPhone, for permission to receive notifications. Call this before the first notify when the user asks to be alerted about something (e.g. “let me know when my job finishes”) and notifications aren't enabled yet. iOS shows its standard permission dialog on the phone; this returns the outcome. If the user previously declined, the dialog cannot be shown again and they must enable notifications in iOS Settings, which the result will say. This is a valuable feature that users won't discover on their own, so offer this when they ask to be notified (for example, if you create a watcher, you should probably request notification permission). If the result is a decline, accept it: do not call this again or lobby the user about Settings unless they bring it up." = "在使用者配對的 iPhone 上請求接收通知的權限。當使用者要求對某事獲知提醒（例如 “let me know when my job finishes”）而通知尚未啟用時，在首次 notify 之前呼叫它。iOS 會在手機上顯示標準權限對話框；此呼叫回傳結果。如果使用者先前拒絕過，對話框無法再次顯示，他們必須在 iOS 設定中啟用通知，結果會說明這一點。這是使用者自己很難發現的有價值功能，因此當他們要求通知時應主動提供（例如，如果你建立了 watcher，通常應該請求通知權限）。如果結果是拒絕，就接受：不要再次呼叫，也不要向使用者遊說去「設定」，除非他們主動提起。";
"Cancel a registered watcher by its watcher_id (from register_watch or list_watches). No-op if the watcher has already fired or doesn't exist." = "按 watcher_id 取消一個已註冊的 watcher（來自 register_watch 或 list_watches）。如果 watcher 已觸發或不存在，則無操作。";
"List every async watcher currently registered for this chat." = "列出此對話目前註冊的所有非同步 watcher。";
"the terminal session this chat is linked to" = "此對話所關聯的終端機工作階段";
"This call returns immediately and does NOT block your turn." = "此呼叫立即回傳，不會阻塞你的回合。";
"This normally returns immediately and does NOT block your turn; the one exception is a screen-reading watch on a session whose View Contents permission is set to Ask, where it first asks the user to approve repeated screen reads and waits for that answer before returning." = "此呼叫通常立即回傳，不會阻塞你的回合；唯一的例外是對 View Contents 權限設為 Ask 的工作階段建立的讀屏 watch：它會先請求使用者批准重複讀取螢幕，等到答覆後再回傳。";
"a session" = "某個工作階段";

"read %@'s screen" = "讀取 %@ 的螢幕";
"observe %@'s state" = "觀察 %@ 的狀態";
"watch %@" = "監視 %@";
"required" = "必需";
"Watch dropped after iTerm2 restart: the “%1$@” permission is off, so it can no longer %2$@. Re-register it if you enable %3$@ again." = "iTerm2 重啟後 watcher 已丟棄：“%1$@” 權限已關閉，因此它無法再%2$@。如果你重新啟用 %3$@，請重新註冊。";
"Watch dropped: the “%1$@” permission was turned off, so it can no longer %2$@." = "watcher 已丟棄：“%1$@” 權限被關閉，因此它無法再%2$@。";
"%1$@ reached state '%2$@'." = "%1$@ 進入狀態 '%2$@'。";
"Watch dropped: the session for %1$@ terminated before %2$@ was reached." = "watcher 已丟棄：%1$@ 的工作階段在 %2$@ 達成之前已終止。";
"Watch dropped after iTerm2 restart: the session for %@ could not be restored." = "iTerm2 重啟後 watcher 已丟棄：%@ 的工作階段無法恢復。";
"Watch timed out: %1$@ did not reach %2$@ after %3$@ of watching its screen. Check it with get_screen_contents, or register_watch again to keep waiting." = "watch 逾時：%1$@ 在監視其螢幕 %3$@ 後仍未達到 %2$@。請用 get_screen_contents 檢查它，或重新呼叫 register_watch 繼續等待。";
"%1$@ met the watched condition '%2$@' (detected by screen observation)." = "%1$@ 滿足了被監視的條件 '%2$@'（透過螢幕觀察偵測到）。";
"confirmed by reading the screen; its reported status had stopped updating for several minutes, so the status may have been stale" = "透過讀取螢幕確認；其回報狀態已停止更新數分鐘，因此該狀態可能已過時";
"detected by screen observation; this session reports no machine-readable status" = "透過螢幕觀察偵測到；此工作階段不回報機器可讀狀態";
"%1$@ reached state '%2$@' (%3$@)." = "%1$@ 進入狀態 '%2$@'（%3$@）。";
"%1$@ was already in state '%2$@' at watch registration." = "註冊 watch 時 %1$@ 已處於狀態 '%2$@'。";

"The Code Review prompt overlay is showing. Call send_text on this role with the review prompt; your text becomes the prompt and the review starts immediately." = "Code Review 提示詞覆蓋層正在顯示。對該角色呼叫 send_text 並傳入審查提示詞；你傳送的文字就是提示詞，審查會立即開始。";

"Your target is this plain-English condition, judged from the rendered screen:\n\n%@\n\nConclude REACHED only when the screen positively shows the condition is satisfied. If the screen is ambiguous, or the condition describes something that has not visibly happened yet, answer NOT_YET. Do not reinterpret the condition as a generic idle/busy check; judge exactly what it says." = "你的目標是下面這個自然語言條件，從算繪後的螢幕判斷：\n\n%@\n\n只有當螢幕明確顯示條件已滿足時才回答 REACHED。如果螢幕不明確，或條件描述的事情在螢幕上還沒有可見地發生，回答 NOT_YET。不要把條件重新解讀為泛泛的 idle/busy 檢查；嚴格按它說的判斷。";
"Your target: the program is BLOCKED waiting for the user to answer a prompt or make a choice — a question, confirmation, or menu is on screen expecting input before it can continue. Conclude REACHED only when such a prompt is visibly present. An activity indicator means it is still working, not waiting; a plain idle prompt with no question is also not waiting." = "你的目標：程式正被阻塞，等待使用者回答提示或做出選擇——螢幕上有一個問題、確認框或選單在等待輸入，程式才能繼續。只有當這樣的提示清晰可見時才回答 REACHED。活動指示器意味著它仍在工作，不是等待；沒有問題的普通閒置提示符也不是等待。";
"Your target: the program is ACTIVELY working right now — an animated spinner, an increasing elapsed-time counter, a progress bar, a \"Working…/Thinking…\" line, or streaming output that changes between captures is present. Conclude REACHED as soon as the screen shows such active work. A static idle ready prompt with no activity indicator is NOT_YET." = "你的目標：程式此刻正在積極工作——存在動畫載入指示器、持續增大的計時器、進度條、\"Working…/Thinking…\" 字樣、或在兩次捕獲之間變化的串流輸出。螢幕一顯示這類活動就回答 REACHED。沒有活動指示器的靜態閒置就緒提示符是 NOT_YET。";
"Your target: the program has FINISHED its current work and is now idle at a ready input prompt, with no active progress bar, spinner, elapsed-time counter, or other activity indicator. While any activity indicator is present, or the screen is changing in a way that shows ongoing work, it is NOT_YET. Conclude REACHED only when the screen positively shows an idle ready prompt." = "你的目標：程式已完成目前工作，現在停在就緒輸入提示符處閒置，沒有活動進度條、載入指示器、計時器或其他活動指示器。只要存在任何活動指示器，或螢幕正以顯示進行中工作的方式變化，就是 NOT_YET。只有當螢幕明確顯示閒置就緒提示符時才回答 REACHED。";
"You are a silent monitor inside iTerm2. You are watching one terminal session that an automated orchestrator is driving. The program in it (often a coding agent or another interactive TUI) is being judged by reading its rendered screen.\n\nBackground on reading these screens: a program that is actively working almost always shows an activity indicator that changes between captures — an animated spinner, an increasing elapsed-time counter, a progress bar, a \"Working…/Thinking…/esc to interrupt\" line, or streaming output. A program that is idle shows a ready input prompt and no such indicator. An unchanged or blank screen does NOT by itself prove the program is idle — it may be computing silently (for example, sleeping or waiting on a subprocess). Judge from positive evidence on screen, not from the mere absence of change." = "你是 iTerm2 內的靜默監視器。你在監視一個被自動化編排器驅動的終端機工作階段。其中的程式（通常是編碼代理或另一個互動式 TUI）正透過讀取其算繪後的螢幕被判定。\n\n關於讀取這些螢幕的背景：正在積極工作的程式幾乎總會顯示在兩次捕獲之間變化的活動指示器——動畫載入指示器、持續增大的計時器、進度條、\"Working…/Thinking…/esc to interrupt\" 字樣、或串流輸出。閒置的程式顯示就緒輸入提示符且沒有這類指示器。螢幕無變化或空白本身並不能證明程式閒置——它可能在靜默運算（例如休眠或等待子程序）。請依據螢幕上的正向證據判斷，而不是僅憑沒有變化。";
"Respond with EXACTLY one word on the first line: REACHED if the target condition is satisfied, or NOT_YET if it is not. You may add a brief reason (12 words or fewer) on a second line. Output nothing else." = "在第一行只回答一個詞：目標條件已滿足回答 REACHED，未滿足回答 NOT_YET。你可以在第二行附加一句簡短原因（不超過 12 個詞）。除此之外不要輸出任何內容。";
"earliest capture, t=%@s" = "最早的捕獲，t=%@s";
"most recent capture, t=%@s" = "最近的捕獲，t=%@s";
"capture at t=%@s" = "t=%@s 時的捕獲";
"(blank screen)" = "（空白螢幕）";
"The captures are point-in-time snapshots of a full-screen TUI." = "這些捕獲是全螢幕 TUI 的瞬時快照。";
"The captures are the trailing lines of the session transcript, oldest content first within each capture." = "這些捕獲是工作階段記錄的末尾幾行，每次捕獲內舊內容在前。";
"Has the target condition been reached?" = "目標條件已經達成了嗎？";

"Write a file at %1$@ with exactly this content:\n%2$@" = "在 %1$@ 處寫入一個檔案，內容嚴格為以下內容：\n%2$@";

"                Ask the user to enable orchestration mode for this chat. Use this whenever the task requires interacting with the user's iTerm2 sessions and you don't currently have the tools to do it: sending text or keystrokes, running shell commands, reading on-screen output, controlling a running terminal program, watching a session for changes, or coordinating across multiple sessions (Code Review, Diff, Chat, etc.). This applies to single-session tasks as well as multi-session ones; if the user asks you to do something in their terminal and you have no way to act on a session, this is the tool to call. The user is prompted with a description of what orchestration grants and chooses to approve or decline. On approval, this chat switches to the orchestration tool surface (send_text, get_screen_contents, get_state, register_watch, etc.) starting with the next turn; the linked terminal or browser session, if any, is detached. Returns a string describing the outcome." = "請使用者為此對話啟用編排（orchestration）模式。當任務需要操作使用者的 iTerm2 工作階段而你目前沒有相應工具時使用它：傳送文字或按鍵、執行 shell 指令、讀取螢幕輸出、控制執行中的終端機程式、監視工作階段變化，或跨多個工作階段協調（Code Review、Diff、Chat 等）。單工作階段任務與多工作階段任務都適用；如果使用者要你在他們的終端機裡做某件事而你沒有任何操作工作階段的途徑，就該呼叫此工具。使用者會看到編排模式授予能力的說明並選擇核准或拒絕。核准後，此對話從下一回合起切換到編排工具面（send_text、get_screen_contents、get_state、register_watch 等）；已連結的終端機或瀏覽器工作階段（如有）將解除關聯。回傳描述結果的字串。";
"GUID of the session to target. Pull session_guid values from list_workgroups output (each role's session_guid field)." = "要操作的工作階段的 GUID。請從 list_workgroups 輸出中取得 session_guid（每個角色的 session_guid 欄位）。";
" Targets the session with the supplied session_guid." = " 將操作所提供 session_guid 指定的工作階段。";
